  "reasoning": "The defendant operated a breakfast shop and mistakenly used a toxic substance (nitrite) as sugar, resulting in food poisoning of 13 customers and the death of one. This constitutes the manufacturing and sale of food that is harmful/toxic, which is covered by the statutory offense of producing and selling harmful food. The primary culpable act is the distribution of a toxic food product, fitting the charge '生产、销售有毒、有害食品'. While the death could also be seen as negligence, the specific food safety offense is more appropriate.",
  "final_answer": "[罪名]生产、销售有毒、有害食品<eoa>"
}

